<wpt lat="28.3488309" lon="83.741957">
    <ele>1522.3</ele>
    <name>Tikhedhunga</name>
    <desc>From Tikhedhunga the trail goes down and crosses the river (Bhurungdi Khola) with a suspension bridge. After this a steep climb on stone stairs start until Uleri. Along the way are several tea houses offering cold or hot drinks.</desc>
    <sym> </sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="28.35605" lon="83.73626">
    <ele>2024.0</ele>
    <name>of the</name>
    <desc>Uleri is a village of the Magar. After Uleri you encounter the first Rhododendron trees.</desc>
    <sym> </sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="28.36342" lon="83.73345">
    <ele>2206.4</ele>
    <name>Banthanti</name>
    <desc>A small village, with tea houses.</desc>
    <sym> </sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="28.38334" lon="83.71172">
    <ele>2539.4</ele>
    <name>Nangethanti</name>
    <desc>A small village, only an hours walk from the end-point Ghorepani.</desc>
    <sym> </sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="28.399951" lon="83.699706">
    <ele>2828.3</ele>
    <name>Ghorepani</name>
    <desc>Ghorepani has many large hotels. The center offers shops, a bakery and a volley ball court. You&apos;ll find the hotels scattered along the hill and ridge.</desc>
    <sym> </sym>
</wpt>
<trk>
    <name>Poon Hill Trek: Tikhedunga to Ghorepani Doerali</name>
